GreenwichAcademy -> SacredHeart[label="23.2 (24.86)
04/22", weight="77", tooltip="NEIRA Girls Fours, Greenwich Academy, Sacred Heart Greenwich, Greenwich Country Day			
Distance: 1400m Conditions: Race order: 3V/4V, 2V, 1V. All events saw sustained 10-12 m.p.h. cross-tailwinds, with racing heading inland with the rising tide. Intermittent rollers plagued the first 250m, with conditions flattening out as races approached the 300m. Throughout the day racing conditions trended calmer, going from rougher chop at the start to mild agitation by the end. Comments: We also ran an exhibition heat before the girls' events of a GCDS Men's 1V4+ and 1N4+, listed under the Fourth Boat category. Greenwich Academy also ran their 4V as an exhibition event in the 3V category.
Many thanks to the other programs for joining Greenwich Academy again this year on the Mianus, and for their coaches' support in making it a successful day!
None", URL="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=7EFDBA1B24E108B582C6EBA3D988CF47&cat=1", random="random"]; 
BerkshireAcademy -> GreenwichAcademy[label="10.8 (12.46)
05/09", weight="90", tooltip="NEIRA Girls Fours, Berkshire v Canterbury, Greenwich Academy, Lyme/Old Lyme, Sacred Heart			
Distance: 1300 M Conditions: Steady rain; occasional very light tailwind; flat water. Comments: Races alternated with boys' races. Order of racing: 3V, 2V, 1V, 4V. Berkshire hotseated a rower from 3V to 4V. To ensure fair racing, the course was shortened from 1500 M due to aggressive weed growth in the starting area. In 3V race, GA caught a boat-stopping crab just short of the finish. This would not have impacted finish order, but may have increased the margin. Kudos to cox'ns in 1V and 2V for managing tight 5-boat starts.
None", URL="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=F58C6BF71D67F028BA2055A66A6FA063&cat=1", random="random"]; 
